Every species should have a distinct silhouette, trunk, branch structure, foliage, and material appearance.

Use procedural geometry, optimized instanced meshes, generated textures, or suitable original 3D assets.

Do not represent every tree using the same geometry with a different color.

Trees should look natural from the normal exploration distance and remain visually interesting when the camera approaches them.

