# 17. 3D PERFORMANCE AND MOBILE OPTIMIZATION

This is a browser-based 3D application. Performance is essential.

The forest must run smoothly on ordinary laptops and smartphones.

Implement:

- InstancedMesh for repeated geometry.
- Shared geometries and materials.
- Efficient tree rendering.
- Level of Detail (LOD).
- Frustum culling.
- Texture compression where supported.
- Efficient shadow settings.
- Adaptive device pixel ratio.
- Limited rendering resolution on low-end devices.
- Reduced foliage density at a distance.
- Lazy loading of assets.
- Efficient animation loops.
- Proper GPU resource disposal.

Do not create thousands of independent meshes unnecessarily.

Avoid expensive real-time shadows on every individual leaf.

Use baked or simplified shading for distant environmental details.

Pause or reduce rendering when the browser tab is hidden.

Provide a reduced-effects mode.

The application must remain usable if the 3D renderer fails.

In that situation, show a functional 2D forest/archive alternative instead of a blank screen.

Target a stable 30–60 FPS depending on device capabilities.

